---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE, withBase } from '../../site';

const title = 'The story behind Dubliners | Irish pub near Sol, Madrid';
const description =
  'Dubliners occupies the former Barragán tailor shop (from 1885) just off Puerta del Sol, painted ceiling intact. Irish pub with NFL, rugby and live sport, international crowd.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/about/" ogImage="/images/mural-hero.jpg">
  <section class="hero hero-compact">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current="About" />
      <h1>The story behind Dubliners</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Dubliners is an Irish pub just off Puerta del Sol, in a historic Madrid premises that still shows its original character.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hero-artwork" aria-label="Painted ceiling">
    <picture>
      <source
        type="image/webp"
        srcset={`${withBase('/images/mural-hero-sm.webp')} 900w, ${withBase('/images/mural-hero.webp')} 1872w`}
        sizes="100vw"
      />
      <img
        class="hero-artwork__img"
        src={withBase('/images/mural-hero.jpg')}
        alt="Historic painted ceiling at Dubliners Madrid"
        width="1872"
        height="1056"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </picture>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>A piece of Madrid history</h2>
      <p>
        Before Dubliners, the premises were home to the historic Barragán tailor shop, established in 1885.
        Part of the original structure and decoration remains today, including its distinctive painted ceiling.
      </p>
      <p class="brand-line"><strong>Where suits were once made, stories are now shared.</strong></p>
      <p>
        Under that same ceiling you’ll now find Madrid locals, travellers and international students —
        an Irish pub just off Puerta del Sol.
      </p>

      <h2>The premises</h2>
      <p>
        From the street you will spot the green Dubliners neon on Calle de Espoz y Mina, a couple of minutes from Puerta del Sol.
        Inside, the room keeps the bones of the old tailor shop: the painted ceiling overhead is the same one Barragán’s customers looked up at.
        We have changed what happens under it, not the ceiling itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Dubliners today</h2>
      <p>
        English-speaking staff, live sport on the screens, and a mix of people who live here and people passing through.
        Many evenings you will hear English, Spanish and several other languages at the same table.
        Studying or new in town? Here is our <a href={withBase('/international-students-pub-madrid/')}>international pub in Madrid</a> page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every Wednesday: Dubliners’ €1 shots promo at the pub.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={withBase('/wednesday-1-euro-shots-madrid/')}>Wednesday €1 shots</a>
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href={SITE.mapsUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Directions</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Sport the Irish-pub way</h2>
      <p>
        A big projector and 8 screens carry the sport that brings our crowd in. On NFL Sundays that means
        <a href={withBase('/nfl-madrid/')}>the NFL in Madrid</a>, listed game by game once confirmed.
        In November it means <a href={withBase('/ireland-rugby-madrid/')}>Ireland rugby Tests</a>, and through the year football, NBA, F1 and more.
        Kick-off times are always in Madrid time on <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a>, and the
        <a href={withBase('/sports-bar-madrid/')}>sports bar page</a> explains how the screens work.
      </p>

      <h2>Open from midday</h2>
      <p>
        We open every day from 12:00, until 02:00 Sunday to Thursday and 02:30 on Friday and Saturday — early enough for a daytime
        drink near Sol and late enough for evening kick-offs. Hours and map: <a href={withBase('/visit/')}>Visit</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Quick facts</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What:</strong> an Irish pub with live sport, in the former Barragán tailor shop (established 1885).</li>
        <li><strong>Where:</strong> Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, a couple of minutes from Puerta del Sol.</li>
        <li><strong>Screens:</strong> a big projector and 8 screens — NFL, rugby, football, NBA, F1 and more.</li>
        <li><strong>Language:</strong> English-speaking staff; English and Spanish spoken at the bar.</li>
        <li><strong>Hours:</strong> every day from 12:00; until 02:00 Sunday–Thursday and 02:30 Friday–Saturday.</li>
        <li><strong>Midweek:</strong> €1 shots every Wednesday.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Find us</h2>
      <p>
        Calle de Espoz y Mina 7<br />
        28012 Madrid
      </p>
      <p>Metro Sol (L1, L2, L3) or Sevilla (L2). Follow us on Instagram: <a href={SITE.instagram} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@dublinersirishpubmadrid</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
